# EtChipsGroupV2 Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtChipsGroupV2` is a group component for displaying and managing selectable chips in the eToro design system. It provides:

- **Data-driven API**: items array prop pattern (like `EtTextToggle`/`TimeFrameSelector`)
- **Three selection modes**: none (display-only), single (radio-like), multi (checkbox-like)
- **Two layout modes**: horizontal scroll with fade overlays, or wrapped multi-row
- **Controlled-only state**: no uncontrolled/defaultValue mode
- **RTL support**: fade overlays automatically flip for right-to-left layouts
- **Haptic feedback**: enabled by default on selection

**Does NOT handle:**

- Uncontrolled state management (always use `value`/`onChange`)
- Navigation logic (use with router/navigation handlers)
- Custom chip variants (uses standard `EtChip` internally)

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtChipsGroupV2` (main component)

```tsx
// Non-selectable mode (display only)
<EtChipsGroupV2
  items: ChipsGroupItem[]          // required
  selectionMode?: 'none'           // default: 'none'
  layout?: 'scroll' | 'wrap'       // default: 'scroll'
  gap?: number                     // default: 8
  fadeColor?: string               // background color for fade (defaults to theme bgNeutralPrimary)
  haptics?: boolean                // default: true
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  contentContainerStyle?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string
/>

// Single selection mode (controlled)
<EtChipsGroupV2
  items: ChipsGroupItem[]
  selectionMode: 'single'
  value: string | null             // required for single mode
  onChange: (value: string | null) => void  // required
  // ... other props
/>

// Multi selection mode (controlled)
<EtChipsGroupV2
  items: ChipsGroupItem[]
  selectionMode: 'multi'
  value: string[]                  // required for multi mode
  onChange: (value: string[]) => void  // required
  // ... other props
/>
```

### `ChipsGroupItem` interface

```typescript
interface ChipsGroupItem {
  id: string; // Unique identifier
  label: string; // Display label
  icon?: IconName; // Optional leading icon
}
```

## Usage Patterns

### Non-selectable (display only)

```tsx
const categories = [
  { id: '1', label: 'Technology' },
  { id: '2', label: 'Finance' },
  { id: '3', label: 'Healthcare' },
];

<EtChipsGroupV2 items={categories} selectionMode="none" />;
```

### Single selection

```tsx
const [selected, setSelected] = useState<string | null>(null);
const filters = [
  { id: 'all', label: 'All' },
  { id: 'stocks', label: 'Stocks' },
  { id: 'crypto', label: 'Crypto' },
];

<EtChipsGroupV2 items={filters} selectionMode="single" value={selected} onChange={setSelected} />;
```

### Multi selection

```tsx
const [selected, setSelected] = useState<string[]>([]);
const tags = [
  { id: 'tech', label: 'Technology' },
  { id: 'finance', label: 'Finance' },
  { id: 'energy', label: 'Energy' },
];

<EtChipsGroupV2 items={tags} selectionMode="multi" value={selected} onChange={setSelected} />;
```

### Wrapped layout

```tsx
<EtChipsGroupV2 items={categories} selectionMode="multi" value={selected} onChange={setSelected} layout="wrap" />
```

### With icons

```tsx
const items = [
  { id: '1', label: 'Favorites', icon: 'heart' },
  { id: '2', label: 'Watchlist', icon: 'watched' },
];

<EtChipsGroupV2 items={items} selectionMode="single" value={selected} onChange={setSelected} />;
```

### Custom fade color (for non-white backgrounds)

```tsx
const { colors } = useEtoroTheme();

// When placed on a gray background, use fadeColor to match
<View style={{ backgroundColor: colors.bgNeutralSecondary }}>
  <EtChipsGroupV2 items={filters} selectionMode="single" value={selected} onChange={setSelected} fadeColor={colors.bgNeutralSecondary} />
</View>;
```

## Anti-patterns

### ❌ Using uncontrolled state

```tsx
// BAD - no defaultValue support, use controlled state
<EtChipsGroupV2
  items={items}
  selectionMode="single"
  defaultValue="1" // This prop doesn't exist!
/>
```

**Fix:** Always provide `value` and `onChange` for single/multi modes:

```tsx
const [selected, setSelected] = useState<string | null>('1');

<EtChipsGroupV2 items={items} selectionMode="single" value={selected} onChange={setSelected} />;
```

### ❌ Missing value/onChange for selectable modes

```tsx
// BAD - single/multi modes require value and onChange
<EtChipsGroupV2
  items={items}
  selectionMode="single"
  // Missing value and onChange!
/>
```

**Fix:** TypeScript will enforce this - always provide both props:

```tsx
<EtChipsGroupV2 items={items} selectionMode="single" value={selected} onChange={setSelected} />
```

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal Dependencies

- `EtChip` - individual chip rendering
- `useChipsGroupConfig` - selection logic hook
- `useScrollFade` - scroll position and overflow detection
- `ScrollFadeOverlay` - animated fade gradient overlays

### External Dependencies

- `expo-haptics` - haptic feedback on selection
- `expo-linear-gradient` - fade overlay gradients
- `react-native` - `ScrollView`, `View`, `Animated`, `I18nManager`

### Design System Integration

- Uses `EtChip` component with all its styling
- Gap default: 8px (matches chip spacing in Figma)
- Fade overlay width: 48px (matches design specs)
- Fade animation: 60fps UI-thread animations using Reanimated SharedValues
- Fade opacity interpolates smoothly based on scroll position (0-20px range)

## Patterns & Pitfalls

### Controlled-Only State

This component is **controlled-only** - no internal state management:

- Single mode: parent manages `string | null`
- Multi mode: parent manages `string[]`
- None mode: no value props needed

### RTL Support

Fade overlays automatically adapt to RTL:

- `position="start"` renders on left (LTR) or right (RTL)
- `position="end"` renders on right (LTR) or left (RTL)
- Gradient direction flips accordingly

### Selection Mode Behavior

| Mode   | Clicking unselected | Clicking selected  | Value type       |
| ------ | ------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------- |
| none   | No action           | No action          | N/A              |
| single | Selects it          | Deselects (null)   | `string \| null` |
| multi  | Adds to array       | Removes from array | `string[]`       |

### Scroll Fade Logic

- Fade overlays are always enabled for scroll layout (automatically hidden when no overflow)
- Start fade: hidden at scroll position 0, fades in over 0-20px scroll
- End fade: shown initially when content overflows, fades out over last 20px of scroll
- No fade overlays appear when content fits within the container (no scrollable content)
- Use `fadeColor` prop when placed on non-white backgrounds to match the container's background color

## Related Context

- `EtChip (chips/)` - Underlying chip component. Use directly for single standalone chips, action chips, or when custom layout is needed
- `EtRadioGroup` - Similar selection pattern (single only)
- `EtTextToggle` - Similar data-driven API pattern
- `TimeFrameSelector` - Similar horizontal selector pattern

### Relationship to EtChip

`EtChipsGroupV2` is a **composite component** that uses `EtChip` internally. It provides:

- Data-driven API (pass `items` array instead of rendering children)
- Built-in selection state management (single/multi/none modes)
- Built-in layouts (horizontal scroll with fade overlays, or wrapped grid)
- Proper accessibility roles for the group (`radiogroup` for single, `group` for multi)

Use `EtChip` directly when you need:

- A single standalone chip
- Action chips (non-selection buttons with `onPress`)
- Custom layout or behavior not covered by `EtChipsGroupV2`
- Flexibility with compound children (custom icon placement)
